1. Agreement, scope and free protections

This agreement governs proprietary portions of the lawfully obtained Vault
Foundations software supplied by ARCXCOVAEL LLC. It applies when presented by
an authorized release and accepted through its identified process. Possessing
a private development or review copy does not authorize distribution.

You may use the supplied early filtering, performance protections, status and
recovery, and existing generated navigation without purchasing full navigation
access. Your notes and ordinary links remain usable and editable independently.
Full access adds ongoing automatic folder, root and optional Home navigation
upkeep. Local processing does not give the company ownership of your vault.

One purchased license covers one named person for personal and internal business
use across devices that person owns or is authorized to use and their vaults.
There is no numeric device or vault limit for that person. It is not a shared
team or household seat. Organizations need a seat for each named person.

2. Your production trial

Your one 30-day production trial starts only when you are signed in, accept
the presented terms and explicitly select "Start 30-day trial". Downloading,
signing in, accepting terms alone, waiting and earlier private testing do not
start it. Reinstalling, changing
devices or vaults, reconnecting and updating do not restart the same account's
original trial. Contact support for an incorrectly recorded start or deadline.

Online activation and periodic trial checks are required. A verified signed
offline allowance lasts up to 24 hours after a successful check and never beyond
the original trial end. The panel shows the next check deadline. A service
outage does not extend that deadline or create unsigned access. Starting a trial
does not create an automatic charge, subscription or payment-card obligation.

3. Purchase and permanent 1.x rights

After a valid purchase, the named person receives permanent, nonexclusive use of
version 1.x and all 1.x updates ARCXCOVAEL LLC releases, including features
released within 1.x. Future major versions starting with 2.0 are optional. A
later subscription or pricing change does not require repurchasing that 1.x
entitlement. This does not promise indefinite development, download hosting,
individual support or compatibility with every future host version.

The Sales and Founding Offer policy states price eligibility and deadlines.
The seller, currency, one-time price, applicable tax, total and sales policies
must be shown before payment. Starting a trial authorizes no automatic purchase.
An already-open, server-created checkout retains its quoted price if payment
completes later; a new checkout uses the eligibility then applicable.

All sales are final. We do not offer discretionary refunds, including
change-of-mind refunds. Use the 30-day trial to evaluate compatibility,
performance and suitability before purchasing. This does not limit mandatory
legal remedies or payment-provider obligations and authority.

A purchased 1.x signed proof does not require recurring server contact. Keep a
lawful backup for your licensed use. Losing a proof or moving without it can
require online account recovery and reasonable purchase evidence. A service
outage does not itself terminate an otherwise valid purchased entitlement.

4. Your content, safe fallback and backups

You retain rights in your notes, vault contents, annotations, configurations and
generated Markdown. This agreement gives the company no ownership of, access to
or right to train on those contents. You may read, edit, retain, export and share
generated folder notes and ordinary links without full navigation access.

Expiry or nonpurchase pauses new paid automation. It does not authorize deleting,
encrypting, corrupting or hiding notes, annotations or generated pages, removing
ordinary editing, or abruptly withdrawing early filtering and performance
protections. An already-admitted transaction may finish before subsequent paid
work pauses. Settings, identities and recovery are preserved. No remote wipe is
authorized.

Maintain independent, current backups of your vault, notes and configuration.
Verify restoration before enabling automated navigation, changing exclusions,
moving generated-output locations or updating. Local recovery supplements your
backup; it does not replace it or waive mandatory legal rights.

